 "method": "Both runners are driven through the PRODUCTION adapter (control_graph.Adapter over control_graph.exchange): the same staging, environment, deadline and answer checks. The step runner is launched as production launches it (the resolved base interpreter, -I -S -B); the LangGraph runner as the adapter launched it before VELDO-0262 (its locked interpreter, -I -B). Samples are interleaved on one host, one runner then the other, for three workloads: the default code definition (control_workflow_unit.CODE), the runtime qualification workflow and a VELDO-0247 fan-out of 4, each a start and an advance. The LangGraph runner's import and graph build time is measured in its own child: python -X importtime over a real exchange, and perf_counter around its imports and its _build of the same workflow.",
